    <item>
      <title>Redraft 0.1.4</title>
      <pubDate>Sun, 04 Oct 2026 05:01:00 GMT</pubDate>
      <sparkle:version>5</sparkle:version>
      <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.1.4</sparkle:shortVersionString>
      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <description><![CDATA[<ul><li>Move a paragraph, a whole section (from its heading) or a list item up and down with ⌥⌘↑ and ⌥⌘↓. Next and previous alternative are now ⌥⌘→ and ⌥⌘←.</li><li>The word count shows how many words you've selected and how long the piece takes to read. Right-click it to set a length target.</li><li>Copy Rich Text (⌥⇧⌘C) pastes into Substack, Ghost, Google Docs or Mail with headings, emphasis and links intact.</li><li>⌘B, ⌘I and ⌘K for bold, italic and links. Paste a web address over selected words to link them. In a list, Return starts the next item and Tab nests it.</li><li>Type TK for anything still to fill in. It's highlighted and counted, and Export Clean Copy reminds you before it goes out.</li><li>Zen dims everything but the paragraph you're writing and keeps your line in the middle of the screen. Turn either off in Settings → Editor.</li><li>Fixes: typing after a file changes on disk is no longer lost; Redo after Stash keeps the passage; files in other encodings open correctly; smart quotes and dashes leave code and --- alone; exports keep line breaks.</li><li>Faster typing in long drafts.</li></ul>]]></description>
      <enclosure url="https://github.com/brettsmith212/redraft/releases/download/v0.1.4/Redraft-0.1.4.dmg" length="6096940" type="application/octet-stream" sparkle:edSignature="hf5TLy3iA2XyEv7U+l6ip3TimcxQe0zcI21nBB9MIVIml7VA8bdBPoBzFHw6AveSfgMOC3EDeyat9noxPXfgCA=="/>
    </item>
